 *exactly* describes my winning move. The "Card Held" count confirms that the landlord has a single card and has already played the 7, so they are guaranteed to go out if I don\'t act. There is no other decision.\n\n**Evaluation:** I have the winning card and a clear path to victory.\n**Reason:** Playing the King of Hearts (♥K) wins the game immediately. It is the only strategic move.\n**Answer:** {"cards": ["♥K"]}\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: I have exactly one card left, the King of Hearts. The Landlord (Previous Player) has just played a single 7 and has only 1 card remaining in their hand. If I can empty my hand, the Peasant team wins immediately. My King beats the 7.\n\nReason: Playing the King empties my hand and secures the win for the Peasant team instantly. Passing is not an option because it would prolong the game when a guaranteed win is available, and it risks the Landlord playing their final card to win on the next opportunity.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥K"]}'}
